{
  "_comment": "THE REPOSITORY ROOT's declaration: what this instance IS and which directories it holds. Its sibling `ihris.config.json` says how it is configured. Written following folio-assistant's cat-harness/docs/bootstrap/initialization.md: declaration first, then only the directories it names.",
  "name": "ihris",
  "title": "iHRIS Knowledge Base",
  "description": "A folio-assistant folio that ingests and DESCRIBES the knowledge assets of iHRIS, the open-source health workforce information system: Launchpad source (by `lp:` reference, never copied), iHRIS 5 on GitHub (pinned by commit), the Implementation Toolkit, the old wiki (and its 2010 handbook export), the 2009 use-case model, the 2011 administrator e-learning course (CC BY 4.0, IntraHealth International), and documents people share. It is the umbrella over one instance per core source repository and one per knowledge source.",
  "avatar": {
    "glyph": "M8 11a3 3 0 100-6 3 3 0 000 6zM16 11a3 3 0 100-6 3 3 0 000 6zM2 20a6 6 0 0112 0M10 20a6 6 0 0112 0",
    "tone": 208,
    "reads": "two people side by side: a health workforce, in iHRIS blue"
  },
  "_avatar_comment": "The harness chrome's mark for ihris (the rail's header, the harness rows) is the iHRIS logo: `icon` names the `mark` image, which cat-harness puts before the glyph. The rail is dark in both schemes and the logo is a black mark, so the image is the logo for a dark ground, white with its shape unchanged: the owner's dark-scheme logo choice (2026-10-09, docs/design/wireframes/dark-scheme/), written by src/tools/derive_dark_theme.py from the verified logo. Its `ground` is `none`: the rail draws it on the rail itself, with no tone square behind it (litlfred/cat-harness#49). The glyph stays as the fallback for a surface that draws no image. Tone 208 is MEASURED from the theme's h1 #1e5483 (src/site/theme/ihris-classic.json): rgb(30,84,131), hue 4 + (30-84)/(131-30) sixths of a turn = 207.9 degrees.",
  "icon": "mark",
  "images": [
    {
      "id": "mark",
      "src": "docs/assets/img/iHRIS_logo-on-dark.svg",
      "role": "mark",
      "width": 62,
      "height": 62,
      "title": "iHRIS logo",
      "description": "The iHRIS logo, (c) IntraHealth International, from the iHRIS 4.3.3 release (GPL), drawn white for a dark ground.",
      "ground": "none"
    }
  ],
  "navbarIcons": [
    "close",
    "beans",
    "launcher"
  ],
  "_navbarIcons_comment": "ihris's OWN icon row, rather than the cat-harness list it would inherit (todos, beans, fsh-guts, launcher). todos and fsh-guts are dashboards of state graphs ihris does not declare, so they drew inert icons reading 'reason not recorded' (owner, 2026-10-09: 'missing icons on navbar top'). beans links to ihris's work plan at /beans/, with its open count (bean ihris-mdzi).",
  "repository": "litlfred/ihris",
  "needs": [
    "folio-assistant-core"
  ],
  "_needs_comment": "A folio-assistant-core DEPENDENT repository, as litlfred/who-iris is (owner, 2026-10-09: 'migrate to new folio-assistant-core dependent repo'). folio-assistant-core is the one instance ihris needs; cat-harness and the rest arrive as its closure. Where each comes from, at which SHA, is index.config.json (pins) and index.lock.json (what they resolved to); src/tools/mount_platform.sh lays them down at <name>/, git-ignored. ihris's tools find them through src/tools/folio_platform.py only.",
  "instances": [
    {
      "name": "i2ce",
      "path": "src/i2ce",
      "kind": "launchpad-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-common",
      "path": "src/ihris-common",
      "kind": "launchpad-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-manage",
      "path": "src/ihris-manage",
      "kind": "launchpad-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-qualify",
      "path": "src/ihris-qualify",
      "kind": "launchpad-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-plan",
      "path": "src/ihris-plan",
      "kind": "launchpad-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "openhie-pr",
      "path": "src/openhie-pr",
      "kind": "launchpad-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris5",
      "path": "src/ihris5",
      "kind": "github-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-toolkit",
      "path": "library/ihris-toolkit",
      "kind": "knowledge-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-wiki",
      "path": "library/ihris-wiki",
      "kind": "knowledge-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-admin-handbook",
      "path": "library/ihris-admin-handbook",
      "kind": "knowledge-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-use-cases",
      "path": "library/ihris-use-cases",
      "kind": "knowledge-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-admin-course",
      "path": "library/ihris-admin-course",
      "kind": "knowledge-source"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-data-dictionary",
      "path": "src/ihris-data-dictionary",
      "kind": "derived-knowledge-asset"
    },
    {
      "name": "ihris-4-on-fhir",
      "path": "src/ihris-4-on-fhir",
      "kind": "derived-knowledge-asset"
    }
  ],
  "_instances_comment": "One instance per core Launchpad repository, per the owner's ruling on issue #1 ('instance for each lp repo'), plus iHRIS 5, the toolkit and the wiki. Core = i2ce, ihris-common, ihris-manage, ihris-qualify, ihris-plan, openhie-pr. The other 31 Launchpad projects (country customizations and side tools) are described in the root catalogue at src/catalogue/ only. ihris-4-on-fhir (2026-09-23) is derived content, and the only subgraph that depends on smart-base. ihris-admin-handbook (the 2010 wiki export, GFDL-1.2) and ihris-use-cases (the 2009 use-case model, owner's permission) were added 2026-09-23 (bean ihris-hbuc). ihris-admin-course (2026-10-09) is the Moodle course backup of iHRIS Administrator - Level I; the backup states no licence, and its author, the owner, stated CC BY 4.0 with attribution to IntraHealth International (2026-10-09), so it is ingested.",
  "assets": [
    {
      "id": "agent-instructions",
      "src": "AGENTS.md",
      "role": "agent-instructions",
      "title": "AGENTS.md: ihris",
      "description": "What a cold agent does here, in order.",
      "source": {
        "instance": "litlfred/bootstrap",
        "path": "AGENTS.md"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "instance-readme",
      "src": "README.md",
      "role": "instance-readme",
      "title": "iHRIS Knowledge Base",
      "description": "What this repository is and what is here."
    }
  ],
  "directories": [
    {
      "id": "uploads",
      "path": "uploads/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "uploads"
      ],
      "description": "The ingestion queue: raw captures exactly as received (Launchpad pages, toolkit pages, GitHub inventories, source-tarball manifests). NOT corpus. Tarballs are git-ignored; their manifests pin them by checksum."
    },
    {
      "id": "ihris-catalogue",
      "path": "src/catalogue/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "catalogue"
      ],
      "readOnly": true,
      "readOnlyBasis": "Generated by src/tools/build_kg.py from uploads/launchpad/. Edit the capture or the script, never the node.",
      "description": "The iHRIS Suite project group on Launchpad and every project in it (plus openhie-pr, openhie, openinfoman), each as a folio-catalogue-node/v1 by reference with an ihris-source-record/v1 companion. Core projects point at their own instance."
    },
    {
      "id": "schemas",
      "path": "src/schemas/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "schemas"
      ],
      "description": "The four schemas this folio adds (ihris-source-record, ihris-i2ce-module, ihris-form-class, ihris-toolkit-stage). Everything else reuses folio-assistant's own.",
      "coverage": {
        "visualiser": [
          {
            "ref": "docs/schemas/index.html",
            "writer": [
              "src/tools/site_instances.py"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "skills",
      "path": "src/skills/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "skills"
      ],
      "description": "The procedures used to build this graph, as skills an agent can repeat."
    },
    {
      "id": "tools",
      "path": "src/tools/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "code"
      ],
      "description": "The scripts that regenerate every derived node, with a Tool node (*.tool.json) for each."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs",
      "path": "docs/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "docs"
      ],
      "description": "Reader-facing documentation about this knowledge base. docs/generated/ is build output."
    },
    {
      "id": "methodologies",
      "path": "methodologies/",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "skills"
      ],
      "description": "Adopted methodologies (folio-methodology/v1), one directory each. wiregen is drafted here provisionally; by methodology-adoption §4 it belongs in the harness (bean ihris-0nml).",
      "dependents": "skip"
    },
    {
      "id": "processes",
      "path": "processes/",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "processes"
      ],
      "description": "BPMN processes GENERATED from processes/specs/*.json by src/tools/gen_bpmn.py. Judgement points call folio-assistant's existing processes (Process_Adjudication, Process_OptionsAnalysis, Process_Ingestion) instead of copying them.",
      "dependents": "skip"
    },
    {
      "id": "glossary",
      "path": "glossary/",
      "dependents": "reproduce",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "glossary"
      ],
      "readOnly": true,
      "readOnlyBasis": "Generated by src/tools/build_glossary.py from library/ihris-toolkit/stages/, library/ihris-use-cases/ and src/*/data-lists/ with the verified ConceptMaps in src/ihris-data-dictionary/terminology/. Edit the inputs or the script, never a scheme.",
      "description": "folio-assistant core's glossary kind: one folio-glossary/v1 SKOS concept scheme per source (the toolkit's technical terms, the 2009 use-case glossaries, and each iHRIS 4.3.3 code list), terms in this instance's namespace, each authored (definition verbatim from the source), candidate (named, no definition) or could-not-extract. External concepts are linked by exactMatch from verified ConceptMaps only, never copied. Rendered on the site's glossary/ page, with SKOS JSON-LD per scheme.",
      "coverage": {
        "visualiser": [
          {
            "ref": "docs/glossary/index.html",
            "writer": [
              "src/tools/site_instances.py",
              "src/tools/build_glossary.py"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library-papers",
      "path": "library/arxiv-2312.07755/",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "library"
      ],
      "description": "Referenced source documents (reference only when the source states no licence): headings, page ranges and a summary in our own words.",
      "dependents": "skip",
      "coverage": {
        "visualiser": [
          {
            "ref": "docs/library/index.html",
            "writer": [
              "src/tools/site_instances.py"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "beans",
      "path": "beans/",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "beans"
      ],
      "coverage": {
        "visualiser": [
          {
            "ref": "docs/beans/index.html",
            "writer": [
              "src/tools/site_instances.py",
              "src/tools/gen_beans_data.ts"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "description": "The work plan: beans/defs/ (.beans.yml, prefix ihris-), with the bean graph beans/beans.json. Published on this folio's site at /beans/ as the platform's own work-plan board, from assets/beans/index.json (src/tools/gen_beans_data.ts, the platform's functions)."
    }
  ],
  "remoteGraphs": [
    {
      "id": "esco-isco-08",
      "url": "http://data.europa.eu/esco/concept-scheme/isco",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "glossary"
      ],
      "title": "ISCO-08 in ESCO (European Commission)",
      "description": "The ILO's ISCO-08 occupation groups as SKOS concepts, published by ESCO: http://data.europa.eu/esco/isco/C + the ISCO-08 code. A code-list term links here by exactMatch from the ValueSet that binds its iHRIS list to the ILO ISCO-08 system (ValueSet identity, accepted by the owner on 2026-09-24), or from a verified ConceptMap to ISCO-08 (none exists yet). Referenced, never held; not dereferenced from the building session."
    },
    {
      "id": "eu-authority-country",
      "url": "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "glossary"
      ],
      "title": "EU Publications Office authority table: countries",
      "description": "Countries as SKOS concepts: http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ + the ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 code. iHRIS country codes link here from ConceptMap country-to-iso-3166 (equal only). Referenced, never held; not dereferenced from the building session."
    },
    {
      "id": "eu-authority-currency",
      "url": "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/currency",
      "graphTypologies": [
        "glossary"
      ],
      "title": "EU Publications Office authority table: currencies",
      "description": "Currencies as SKOS concepts: http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/currency/ + the ISO 4217 code. iHRIS currency codes link here from ConceptMap currency-to-iso-4217 (equal only). Referenced, never held; not dereferenced from the building session."
    }
  ],
  "_visualiser_comment": "WHERE A GRAPH IS SEEN on this folio's own site, so the rail links to ihris's page rather than reading 'no viewer yet': the work-plan board at /beans/ (bean ihris-mdzi), the glossary, the schemas index and the library. This folio's site is GENERATED (src/tools/build_site.py into _site/, published at /ihris/), so `docs/<page>` names the published page and `writer` its generator. ihris is the root of its checkout, so cat-harness publishes these at its site root and keeps them on its own site (litlfred/cat-harness#46, fixed by #49)."
}
